{
  "title": "Dawn Along the River",
  "details": "Soft light spilled across the water as her feet met the dew-damp path. Her breath curled in the cool air, timing with the rhythm of each step. Reeds swayed gently, whispering secrets to the current. A kingfisher darted low, blue wings flashing like a shard of sky fallen to earth."
}

- She paused beside a moss-covered log, watching ripples chase one another downstream
- The river’s quiet song wove through the stillness, punctuated only by the distant call of a waking heron
